what: Compare quarantine and tenant-erasure auditError conventions under real injected ledger failures
run: focused erasure and quarantine tests plus inspected semantic comparison
date: 2026-09-03T13:17:45Z
inspection: TenantErasureReceipt and QuarantineReviewReceipt both expose optional auditError and omit mutationId when recordMutation fails.
inspection: Both preserve the already-durable primary state change and surface the ledger error message; erasure additionally reports status=partial because its status denotes whole-operation completeness, while quarantine retains promoted/rejected because its status denotes the durable review decision.
inspection: field naming and ledger-gap semantics are consistent; the domain-specific status distinction is explicit and non-blocking.

